<Defs>

  <!--
    The Helix Works (docs/design/peoples-third.md, the fifth of the eight; docs/design/peoples.md, "Release G";
    Source/ColonyCouncil/Peoples/PeoplesG.cs): a guild of geneticists who outlived the lab that made them and kept working,
    most of them their own work. Spacer, on the game's outlander parent; they arise in the industrial and spacer ages
    (ariseAges 2~3: gene work wants the means) and are at the height of the ages already (ageLimit 3; cut off from the
    world they fall back to the industrial age like any people). The signature: the lab coat in clinic mint (Anomaly's lab
    coat, Vanilla Apparel Expanded's), over a mint collar shirt with the helix pin; what is under it varies freely. The
    lab guard in recon armour of the same mint with charge rifles (and Rimsenal's spacer pistols under the same tag); a
    mechanitor or two among them (Biotech's mechlink and headset). Mostly not baseliners at all, drawn from every kind of
    people in the player's mods (the one people of Rimfolk's with more of other kinds than baseliners): Biotech's, Odyssey's,
    Alpha Genes', the Vanilla Races Expanded, Rimsenal's, the boglegs', Avaloi, Venators, stoneborn, korgs, the apes',
    the fairies' and the Paws of Interest's. Gifts: genes put in by their own hands (quick study, strong immunity, fast
    wound healing, robust), a psylink now and then (Harmonist, Empath), and a chronomancer of A RimWorld of Magic for a
    chief editor. Their towns: the gene lab, the vat hall and a quiet garden (Rimfolk_Plan_HelixLab). At the gate: a sample
    from a colonist with rare genes, a small blood draw shown (Rimfolk_Evt_HelixSample); gene work, one of their genes
    written into a colonist (Rimfolk_Evt_HelixGeneWork); the vat-keeper's case of medicine and drugs, their trade without
    Biotech too (Rimfolk_Evt_HelixCase); a batch gone wrong asking the colony's help (Rimfolk_Evt_HelixBatch). Their ask:
    genepacks, or medicine without Biotech (Rimfolk_Mission_HelixGenepacks). Their founding: Orla Venn kept the vats warm.
    Faith (Ideology): every body a draft (transhumanist), Vanilla Ideology Expanded's progressive and healthcare.
  -->

  <FactionDef ParentName="OutlanderFactionBase">
    <defName>Rimfolk_HelixWorks</defName>
    <label>Helix Works</label>
    <description>A guild of geneticists who outlived the lab that made them, and kept working. Most of them are their own work: their bodies written and rewritten by the hands of the ones before, so that hardly any two of them are the same kind of person. They sell gene work and medicine, buy genepacks, and pay well for a sample of anything rare.\n\nTheir ways began when the lab's founders fled a plague in the vats and left the vats running. The eldest of the lab's own grown, Orla Venn, kept the vats warm through the winter and read the founders' notes aloud to the others they had made. She taught them to edit what they were given, each one writing the next, and called the lab the Helix Works. Her genome is the first entry in the Works' ledger, with every change she made to it.\n\nThey are curious, patient and exact, and they ask before they change anything. They fear a batch gone wrong, a change made without asking and the vats going cold. A lab is run by its sequencer, and the Works by their chief editor.</description>
