    <fixedIdeo>true</fixedIdeo>
    <ideoName>The Living Draft</ideoName>
    <ideoDescription>Every body is a draft, and the Works are only editors. A body is given, not chosen, and the kindest thing one person can do for another is to ask what they would change and help them change it. Orla Venn, the eldest of the lab's own grown, kept the vats warm when the founders fled and read their notes aloud to the others they had made, and every editor since has written into the ledger what they changed and why. Nothing is changed without asking, and a change is always marked.</ideoDescription>
