  <!-- ===================== Their people ===================== -->

  <!--
    How alike they look (docs/design/peoples.md, "Release G"): the lab coat in clinic mint over a mint collar shirt, the
    helix pin on the collar, is the Works' signature; under it, and on the lab hands who wear only the shirt, whatever the
    lab's lockers held (the game's and the mods' everyday clothes, tool belts, glasses). The vat-keeper adds Vanilla
    Apparel Expanded's surgical mask, the guard recon armour of the same mint over the shirt, the mechanitor Biotech's
    airwire headset over a mechlink. In another age the guard take the age's issue (ageArms): plate and spears in the
    medieval age, flak and rifles in the industrial age. Without any mod: the game's shirts, trousers, recon armour, charge
    rifles and pistols, and the shirt's mint.
  -->
  <PawnKindDef Name="Rimfolk_HelixWorksKindBase" Abstract="True">
    <race>Human</race>
    <defaultFactionDef>Rimfolk_HelixWorks</defaultFactionDef>
    <chemicalAddictionChance>0.02</chemicalAddictionChance>
    <invNutrition>2.55</invNutrition>
